Upstream origin: v0.26.3, commit cd12121.

Derived portions (MIT, (c) 2026 Ruslan Grinev):
  - The Telegram bot layer: grammY wiring, middleware, command routing,
    callback handling, inline keyboards and menus.
  - Message rendering, streaming/pinned-message handling and formatting.
  - The i18n string catalogues and the CLI entry point shape.
  - Test harness structure and tooling configuration.

New in this repository:
  - src/reasonix/: the agent backend. An implementation of the client surface
    the bot consumes, on top of the Reasonix `reasonix serve` HTTP+SSE API.
    Contains no upstream code.
  - The per-project serve instance registry.
  - Support for the Reasonix session lease model (watching vs driving a
    session that a local Reasonix runtime owns).

The upstream project remains the reference for the bot layer's behaviour and
is the place to send bug reports about that layer.